## WU-4 — step-up / third-factor reachability from `/api/v1/capabilities/request`
- [x] Re-verified baselines: jest 908 passed / 921 total; tsc 809 errors (4 in `plus/api/server.ts`)
- [x] Root cause confirmed: the route went body-validation → issuer, never read `entitlementRepo`, never called `riskEngine`, never consulted a challenge, and its DTO had no `challengeRequired` field; `CapabilityIssuer.issue` has no decision logic (the decision lives in `AdaptiveRiskEngine.makeDecision`, never invoked by any route)
- [x] `plus/domain/services/challenge.ts`: `ChallengeBinding`, `sameBinding`, `findOutstandingChallenge`, `findCompletedChallenge`; `createChallenge` REUSES an outstanding challenge for the same binding (one binding → one challenge → one email)
- [x] `plus/api/server.ts`: `authorizeCapabilityRequest` gate before signing (entitlement → closed → operation → unknown user → risk → client `riskScore` floor → deny/challenge/allow); challenge response `200 {success:false, challengeRequired:true, challengeId, challengeExpiresAt}`; deny `403`
- [x] `plus/api/server.ts` ctor: ONE signing key for issuer + challenge service (was two independent generated keys → `/api/v1/crypto/public-key` and `/challenges/verify` disagreed, every PIN-verified capability was unusable by Core); singletons reset so this ctor owns the key
- [x] `src/background/auditor.ts` `handleStartStepUp`: resolves `releaseShareRef` from `cybervault_cred_records`, fails `BINDING_NOT_MANAGED` when absent, sends the release-share reference as `resourceId`/`secretRef` (Core pins `expected.resourceId = requestedSecretRef`, so `fetchPlusMaterial` had to stay as-is)
- [x] `tests/extension/step-up-wiring.test.ts`: records merge instead of overwrite, probe binding now has its own managed record, trigger body asserted as the real wire shape (`ref-probe`), new test for `BINDING_NOT_MANAGED`
- [x] New `tests/plus/capability-request-step-up.test.ts` — real `PlusApiServer` on an ephemeral port, real risk engine / challenge service / issuer, in-memory repos + recording email service; 12 tests (challenge gate, binding, reuse+one email, closed/benign/hostile/disallowed/no-entitlement, PIN wrong+limit, PIN correct → verifies against `/api/v1/crypto/public-key`, proven challenge unlocks assurance 3, foreign challenge id denied)
- [x] `jest.config.js`: narrow `diagnostics.exclude: ["**/plus/api/server.ts"]` — required, otherwise ts-jest refuses to compile any test that imports the real route (its 4 pre-existing errors are re-reported). `tsc --noEmit` still covers the file. Disclosed, not widened.
